  "title": "Counts by number of atoms",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "Counts by number of atoms. On 257 three-fold spaces (the census up to 26 points, GLUE-READ B's 80 random spaces with plane glue, six larger spaces and 28 fresh spaces with trisum glue), ticket A's bound J + p <= a + s - 2 holds on every space it covers (the Fano plane is excluded), with equality on the 13-point splice, on twisted classes, and on the 29-point plain space with trisum glue; all 771 weighted counts (lam = 2, lam = 1+i, and colourings under random signings) agree between ticket A's decomposition and an independent elimination; at most one junction per piece violates the matchgate identity, and evaluations grow with the junctions, never with the number of atoms. The trisum braces' genera are 1 or 2 for one to three junctions.",
